{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress internally, reducing electrode swelling. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 capacity, 90.2% initial efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with 13.1% thickness expansion after 50 cycles. This approach enables scalable production and stable cycling in high-energy batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress internally, reducing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The design reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables 80% capacity retention in 1200 cycles for NCM811 pouch cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore engineering as a scalable strategy for mechanically stable silicon-carbon anodes in high-energy lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. The resulting atlas identified 100+ brain cell subclasses and defined active, primed, and repressive chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 mark distinct repressive mechanisms. This resource enables deep learning models for predicting cell-type-specific epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas spans over 100 brain cell subclasses using integrated epigenomic profiling across 2.5 million nuclei",
    "Active chromatin states defined by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal resource provides a comprehensive framework for annotating the brain regulatory genome and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through cell-type-specific epigenomic features."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates why early humans settled only briefly in specific regions of the Arabian desert despite abundant water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Rub' al Khali, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable stone at 55 of 125 sites with palaeolake deposits. The results indicate that early human settlement was constrained by the availability of stone for tool production, not water alone, suggesting a dual requirement for water and lithic resources.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable stone were found at 55 of 125 sites with palaeolake deposits",
    "Spatial modeling shows 57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone",
    "Convergent patterns across Africa, North America, and Asia indicate lithic availability as a universal constraint"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic resource availability, alongside water, critically constrained early human dispersal in arid regions, challenging models that prioritize water alone."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and IL-23-driven gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to enhance tissue-protective functions, while IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion reduced ILC3 numbers and increased enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive intestinal inflammation through PRKAR1A modulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study experimentally identifies a chiral magnon in manganese telluride (MnTe), an altermagnetic material. Using circular-dichroism resonant inelastic x-ray scattering, researchers observed momentum-dependent spin polarization consistent with altermagnetic g-wave symmetry. The findings demonstrate how altermagnetic order influences spin dynamics, potentially advancing spintronic and quantum technologies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Direct experimental evidence for a ch: chiral altermagnon in MnTe",
    "Momentum-dependent spin polarization consistent with altermagnetic g-wave symmetry",
    "Polarization-resolved data confirm discrete magnetic excitations in altermagnetic order"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery establishes a chiral magnon in altermagnetic materials, providing new insights into spin dynamics governed by altermagnetic symmetry."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during processing. The research identifies outward solvent evaporation delaying α-phase conversion at the buried interface, causing kinetic mismatch that worsens moisture damage. A self-segregating molecule (NFA) was designed to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and create a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved 24.84% power conversion efficiency in small cells and maintained 96.26% efficiency after 1000 hours of damp aging at 85% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture damage",
    "Self-segregating NFA molecule synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated somatic copy number variants (CNVs) in human cortical neurons across development using single-cell whole-genome sequencing. Analysis of 2,357 neurons revealed 25.9% of prenatal cortical neurons had widespread CNVs, which decreased 4.5-fold postnatally. Perinatal elimination of neurons with high CN:CNV burdens occurred, likely linked to programmed cell death, with surviving neurons showing depletion of dosage-sensitive genes and neurodevelopmental disorder genes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "25.9% of prenatal cortical neurons exhibited widespread copy number variants",
    "Perinatal elimination reduced CNV-positive neurons by 4.5-fold postnatally",
    "Surviving neurons showed depletion of dosage-sensitive genes and neurodevelopmental disorder genes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates a perinatal genome quality-control mechanism eliminating neurons with aberrant genomes, providing insights into how genetic instability is managed during human neurodevelopment."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how patent scope affects innovation by analyzing the relationship between patent claims and disclosed technical information. The research suggests that patents with broader claims than disclosed technical details could hinder future innovation by limiting opportunities for rival innovators. The findings indicate that narrowing patent claims to align with disclosed disclosures may facilitate competitive innovation without compromising patent protection.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Patents claiming more than they disclose restrict innovation opportunities for rival developers",
    "Narrowing patent claims to match disclosed technical information enables competitive innovation",
    "Overly broad patents may impede future innovation by creating barriers for alternative solutions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides evidence that patent claim scope must align with technical disclosure to optimize innovation pathways, contributing to a more efficient patent system that balances protection and accessibility."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of fabricating nanocomposites with high nanofiller loadings and ordered nanostructures using additive manufacturing. It introduces shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing, which aligns nanomaterials like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes under high shear forces. The approach enables scalable production of macroscopic composites with complex geometries, achieving 55 wt% boron nitride loading in polylactic acid. Post-sintering yields materials with zero volume shrinkage, exceptional thermomechanical stability, and tailored thermal properties: vertically aligned structures show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K), horizontally aligned ones provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K), and BN membranes exhibit robust mechanical strength (3.4 MPa).",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing achieves 55 wt% boron nitride loading in polylactic acid filaments",
    "Post-sintering composites exhibit zero volume shrinkage and thermomechanical stability up to polymer decomposition temperatures",
    "Vertically aligned BN composites show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) while horizontally aligned structures provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This method enables scalable fabrication of nanocomposites with high nanofiller loadings and long-range ordered nanostructures, advancing cross-scale design for thermal management and structural applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how genetic variants influence single-cell chromatin accessibility and disease risk using 3.5 million peripheral blood mononuclear cells from 1,042 donors. It identified 243,225 chromatin accessibility quantitative trait loci (caQTLs), 60% cell-type specific, and demonstrated their role in 16 diseases and 44 blood traits through colocalization with eQTLs. The findings highlight cell-type-specific and state-dependent genetic effects on immune function and disease mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "243,225 chromatin accessibility quantitative trait loci (caQTLs) identified across 28 immune cell types",
    "60% of caQTLs are cell-type specific, with 38,161 peaks linked to rare variants",
    "caQTLs colocalize 4.5-22.6% more disease and trait signals than eQTLs alone"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cell-type-specific chromatin accessibility as a critical layer of genetic regulation influencing immune disease mechanisms, advancing multi-omics integration for complex trait analysis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the structural integrity of the central nervous system (CNS) following a specific experimental procedure. The researchers exposed a whole CNS to assess its resilience. The findings indicate that the CNS maintains structural integrity without significant damage, suggesting robustness under the applied conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The central nervous system remains structurally intact after full exposure",
    "No significant damage was observed in the exposed central nervous system",
    "The CNS demonstrates resilience under the experimental conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides evidence for the central nervous system's structural resilience, contributing to understanding its mechanical stability in specific experimental contexts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting systems. A highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst was developed using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieves stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides to date. The findings highlight enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers as key mechanisms for overcoming this bottleneck.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieves stoichiometric pure water splitting with 0.72% apparent quantum yield at 420 nm",
    "Incompatibility between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting cocatalysts causes photocorrosion and N2 generation",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers facilitate hole extraction and accelerate surface reaction kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting over nitride-based materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing efficient solar-driven water splitting systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used computational simulations of the Drosophila ventral nerve cord connectomes to identify a central pattern generator (CPG) for fly walking. By screening descending neurons, researchers pinpointed DNg100 as a key command neuron driving rhythmic leg movements. Simulations revealed a minimal three-neuron circuit—comprising one inhibitory and two excitatory interneurons—that generates coordinated leg rhythms across all six legs and is necessary and sufficient for rhythmic motor output. The findings provide cellular and synaptic details of a CPG circuit for walking in flies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "DNg100, a descending neuron, acts as the primary command neuron driving rhythmic leg motor activity in walking flies.",
    "A minimal three-neuron circuit (one inhibitory, two excitatory interneurons) generates coordinated leg rhythms across all six legs and is necessary and sufficient for rhythmic motor output.",
    "Optogenetic validation confirmed a separate descending pathway (DNb08) also drives rhythmic leg movements in behaving flies."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies the cellular and synaptic architecture of a minimal central pattern generator circuit for rhythmic leg movements in Drosophila, advancing understanding of how simple neural circuits produce coordinated locomotion."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how preterm birth disrupts cerebellar development by examining intrinsic gestational timing. Using neuroimaging, neurodevelopmental outcomes, and spatial-transcriptomic profiling, researchers found that cerebellar growth and function correlate with gestational age, not postmenstrual age. Key findings include incomplete granule cell maturation and impaired Purkin: cell structural refinement, indicating lineage-specific developmental asynchrony due to prematurity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cerebellar growth and functional outcomes scale with gestational age despite perinatal exposures",
    "Incomplete granule cell maturation",
    "Impaired Purkinje cell structural refinement"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that prematurity causes biologically displaced maturation, revealing cerebellar developmental trajectories are governed by intrinsic gestational timing rather than postmenstrual age."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a pH-activatable nanozyme, SPMMP. It targets breast cancer bone metastasis by disrupting cancer cell metabolic reprogramming and tumor microenvironment. The nanozyme, composed of Prussian blue core, disulfide-bridged mesoporous silica, and manganese oxide shell, releases silicon and alendronate to reduce osteoclast activity. It enhances reactive oxygen species production, depletes glutathione, and suppresses tumor growth in mouse models without significant toxicity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SPMMPA suppresses tumor growth and osteolysis in breast cancer bone metastasis mouse models",
    "The nanozyme enhances reactive oxygen species production and glutathione depletion via pH-responsive catalysis",
    "Alendronate and silicon release reduce osteoclast activity, preserving bone structure"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a pH-responsive catalytic strategy that simultaneously disrupts tumor energy metabolism and maintains bone homeostasis in breast cancer bone metastasis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how semiconductor materials can circumvent Kirchhoff's reciprocity principle limiting solar energy conversion. Using bismuth sulfide, the researchers identified a pseudo-direct bandgap structure with a lower-energy indirect transition and a direct transition elevated by a few kBT. This configuration delays bimolecular electron-hole reusing, enhancing absorption and enabling potential improvements in solar energy conversion beyond Planck's law constraints.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Bismuth sulfide exhibits a pseudo-direct bandgap with a direct transition positioned several kBT above a lower-energy indirect transition",
    "This pseudo-direct bandgap structure significantly delays bimolecular electron-hole recombination compared to classic direct semiconductors",
    "The combination of high absorption and delayed recombination enables solar energy conversion beyond Planck's law limitations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery of a pseudo-direct bandgap in bismuth sulfide demonstrates a mechanism to circumvent Kirchhoff's reciprocity principle, potentially enabling more efficient solar energy conversion by overcoming fundamental limits imposed by Planck's law."
}

{
  "summary": "This study employed machine learning to identify previously unrecognized multilayer MXenes, enabling the rapid synthesis of seven new MXenes via a self-propagating high-temperature method. It also discovered 11 rare earth-based MXenes, revealing semiconducting and magnetic properties across the expanded family. The approach demonstrates a scalable data-driven strategy for accelerating materials discovery while expanding the known MXene chemical space.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of 33 previously synthesized but unrecognized MXene candidates through database mining",
    "Rapid synthesis of seven multilusing a self-propagating high-temperature method requiring no sustained external heating",
    "Discovery of 11 previously unexplored rare earth-based MXenes with semiconducting and magnetic properties"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a data-driven approach for efficiently expanding the MXene family and accelerating sustainable materials discovery through scalable synthesis methods."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines rare earth element (RE3+) integration into proteins and functional materials, focusing on how RE3+ coordination enhances protein rigidity, stability, and secondary structure transitions. It explores the programmability of amino acid sequences to modulate optical, magnetic, and mechanical properties. The study identifies challenges in molecular mechanism analysis and systematic design strategies, emphasizing the need for rational approaches to advance RE3+-protein applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "RE3+ coordination increases protein rigidity and stability",
    "Amino acid sequence programmability modulates optical and magnetic properties",
    "RE3+ incorporation enhances mechanical properties and adhesion strength"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes foundational insights into RE3+-protein interactions, providing critical frameworks for designing functional materials with tunable physical properties across optics, magnetics, and mechanics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how genetic variants, both common and rare, influence single-cell immune gene expression using 5 million cells across 28 immune types and 1,925 individuals' whole-genome data. It identifies regulatory variants for 83% of genes and rare-variant signals for .47% of them, revealing cell-type-specific effects where half of genetic impacts are confined to single cell types or states.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identified regulatory variants for 83% of 21,404 genes tested",
    "Detected rare-variant signals for 47% of genes",
    "Half of genetic effects are cell-type-specific, observed in only one or a few cell types"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a comprehensive framework for mapping cell-type-specific genetic regulation of gene expression, advancing understanding of how genetic variants influence immune cell states and disease mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated spatiotemporal coordination mechanisms during human urogenital system codevelopment using high-resolution spatial transcriptomics and single-cell multiomics on embryos from Carnegie stages 15 to 2:15. It identified mesonephros-derived signals promoting gonadal specification, a potential mesonephric origin of gonadal supporting cells, and three distinct steroidogenic lineages with specialized roles in sex differentiation. These findings advance understanding of urogenital system assembly and multiorgan developmental coordination.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Mesonephros-derived signals promote gonadal specification",
    "Potential mesonephric origin of gonadal supporting cells via rete testis or ovarii",
    "Three transcriptionally distinct steroidogenic lineages with specialized cholesterol sourcing, cortisol synthesis, and sex hormone production"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides mechanistic insights into the coordinated development of the human urogenital system, revealing how spatially distinct cell populations interact to establish sex differentiation pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates thermoelectric-electrocatalytic coupling to enhance oxygen evolution reaction (OER) efficiency using a RuO2/PrCoO3 heterointerface. By integrating thermoelectric oxide PrCoO3 with RuO2, the system leverages thermal gradients to activate inert RuO2 facets, reducing OER overpotential by 43% at 10 mA cm-2 and increasing current density by 300%. The approach demonstrates stable performance in water electrolysis under mild temperature gradients.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Thermoelectric potential from PrCoO3 activates inert RuO2 (101) facets, lowering *OOH formation barrier",
    "OER overpotential reduced by 43% at 10 mA cm-2 with 300% current density increase under 175°C gradient",
    "Stable electrolyzer operation at 2.18 V for 600 hours using spontaneous heating"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a thermoelectric-electrocatalytic coupling strategy that converts waste heat into electrochemical energy, advancing sustainable energy conversion systems through integrated thermal and catalytic mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study estimates Africa-wide water demand for 2020 across six sectors at high spatial resolution, integrating heterogeneous datasets to produce harmonized values. Total annual demand was 347 km³, with irrigation (65%) and municipalities (17%) as dominant sectors. Demand increased by 26% from 2010 to 2020. The analysis highlights regional variations where demand exceeds availability, indicating that physical water availability alone does not ensure water security.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Total annual water demand for Africa in 2020 was 347 km³, with irrigation accounting for 65% (225 km³).",
    "Municipal water demand represented 17% (60 km³) of total demand, with significant uncertainty in key parameters.",
    "Demand increased by 26% between 2010 and 2020, and regional variations exist where water demand exceeds availability despite physical water abundance."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides a spatially and sectorally resolved baseline for understanding water-demand pressures across Africa, clarifying that physical water availability alone does not determine water security."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates stimulated protein degradation (SPD) as a therapeutic strategy for neurodegenerative disorders. SPD uses agonists of stress-responsive E3 ubiquitin ligases to eliminate multiple pathogenic proteins. The approach improved mitochondrial function and neuronal survival in models of neurodegenerative COX deficiency syndrome and Friedreich's atusing E3 ligase activation to enhance cellular integrity. The findings demonstrate SPD's potential for treating conditions with pervasive protein dysregulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SPD leverages E3 ubiquitin ligase agonists to degrade multiple pathogenic proteins",
    "CUL2FEM1B activators enhanced mitochondrial import and electron transport chain assembly",
    "SPD preserved neuronal survival in neurodegenerative COX deficiency syndrome and Friedreich's ataxia models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "SPD provides a mechanism to target multiple pathogenic proteins via E3 ligase activation, offering a novel therapeutic approach for disorders with pervasive protein dysregulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing alkaline hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) catalysts by integrating anti-poisoning tin single-atoms into ruthen. The catalyst, Sn-doped RuO2@Ru on carbon, improves water dissociation kinetics, optimizes hydrogen binding, and prevents hydroxide poisoning. It achieves low overpotential (9 mV at 10 mA cm-2) and stable operation in full electrolyzers at 1.85 V and 1000 mA cm-2 for over 300 hours.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Sn-doped RuO2@Ru catalyst on carbon black demonstrates exceptional HER activity with 9 mV overpotential at 10 mA cm-2",
    "The catalyst prevents *OH poisoning and optimizes *H binding energy through atomic-level electronic modulation",
    "Integration into AEMWE systems achieves stable operation at 1.85 V and 1000 mA cm-2 for over 300 hours"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes atomic-level electronic engineering with anti-poisoning strategies as a viable approach for designing highly active and stable alkaline HER electrocatalysts, advancing industrial hydrogen production technologies."
}
